---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { profile } from '../content/profile';
import '../styles/traffic-pages.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Maternal Health Clinical Research and Telemonitoring Experience"
  description="Review Reeja Maharjan's clinical research experience supporting maternal-health telemonitoring, HDP and GDM workflows, participant education, home BP/BG monitoring, study documentation, data quality, and escalation coordination."
>
  <div class="traffic-page">
    <section class="traffic-hero">
      <div class="container traffic-hero__grid">
        <div>
          <p class="traffic-eyebrow">Maternal-health clinical research experience</p>
          <h1>Registered nursing experience applied to clinical research and telemonitoring.</h1>
          <p class="traffic-lede">A privacy-safe overview of Reeja Maharjan's work supporting the IISH MOM-HD maternal telemonitoring trial through participant screening, home BP/BG monitoring education, follow-up, warning-symptom review, study documentation, data-quality checks, and multidisciplinary coordination.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="traffic-summary">
          <h2>Current research focus</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>MOM-HD maternal telemonitoring trial</li>
            <li>Hypertensive disorders of pregnancy and gestational diabetes workflows</li>
            <li>Home blood-pressure and blood-glucose monitoring education</li>
            <li>Participant follow-up, documentation, and data quality</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="traffic-section">
      <div class="container traffic-split">
        <div class="traffic-section__heading">
          <p class="traffic-eyebrow">Clinical research responsibilities</p>
          <h2>Participant support, accurate study records, and protocol-based coordination</h2>
          <p>Reeja supports maternal-health implementation research by connecting clinical understanding with clear participant communication, safe monitoring routines, careful documentation, and timely escalation to the appropriate clinical team.</p>
        </div>
        <dl class="traffic-facts">
          <div><dt>Participant screening</dt><dd>ANC participant screening, eligibility workflow support, informed-consent process assistance, and organised screening records.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Home monitoring education</dt><dd>Practical teaching on automatic blood-pressure devices, glucometer use, blood-glucose testing, safe recording, and mobile reporting.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Tele-follow-up and escalation</dt><dd>Review of submitted BP/BG readings, warning-symptom screening, follow-up communication, and escalation according to study protocol.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Study documentation and data quality</dt><dd>Digital-platform review, REDCap-style data-quality checks, confidentiality, device logistics, and communication across clinical, research, and technical teams.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="traffic-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="traffic-section__heading">
          <p class="traffic-eyebrow">Relevant capabilities</p>
          <h2>Skills relevant to implementation research, NGOs, INGOs, and health programmes</h2>
          <p>The work is especially relevant to teams that need a clinically trained professional who can communicate with participants, maintain dependable records, support monitoring workflows, and coordinate safely across disciplines.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="traffic-grid">
          <article class="traffic-card"><h3>Participant education and adherence support</h3><p>Explaining monitoring schedules, device use, reporting routines, warning signs, and follow-up requirements in clear language for participants and families.</p></article>
          <article class="traffic-card"><h3>Clinical and multidisciplinary coordination</h3><p>Communicating with nurses, obstetricians, hospital staff, researchers, and technical teams when readings, symptoms, documentation, or escalation require attention.</p></article>
          <article class="traffic-card"><h3>Ethical documentation and confidentiality</h3><p>Maintaining accurate study records and participant privacy without publishing confidential data, study documents, or identifiable health information.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="traffic-section traffic-dark">
      <div class="container traffic-split">
        <div>
          <p class="traffic-eyebrow">Clinical research recruitment</p>
          <h2>Discuss a maternal-health research, clinical study, NGO, or INGO opportunity.</h2>
          <p>Share the organisation, role title, project focus, location, contract period, expected start date, and core responsibilities.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="traffic-actions">
          <a class="traffic-button" href="/hire-reeja/">View recruiter profile</a>
          <a class="traffic-button" href="/cv/">Download nursing CV</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
